    "result_text": "Credit notes now reduce what an invoice and its client still owe. `bin/e2e` builds and the acceptance test passes: an invoice of $100 with a $30 credit shows `$70.00` in `invoice-due-amount`.\n\nNo database migration was needed. The `credit_note` table already existed (V53), but nothing used it when working out amounts owed.\n\n**Server**\n- **Invoice amount due:** this is now the invoice amount minus payments minus credits. That covers the project's invoice list, the client statement, and the responses from the send and cancel actions.\n- **Client amount owed:** credits on sent and part-paid invoices are now subtracted. This feeds the client list, the dashboard's outstanding totals and its top clients.\n- **Payments:** a payment can no longer exceed what's left after credits. An invoice is marked paid once payments plus credits cover its total.\n- **Test seed:** `/__test__/seed` now accepts `creditNotes`, which the test needed.\n\n**Front end**\n- On the invoice detail page, \"Balance due\" now subtracts credits as well as payments, and it updates when a new credit note is raised. No `data-testid` values were renamed or removed.\n\n**Things you might want to change:**\n- **Statement \"paid\" figure:** this total is worked out as invoiced minus outstanding, so it now includes credits as well as real payments. If you want credits shown separately, that needs a new field.\n- **Raising credit notes:** I didn't change this rule. Credits still only can't add up to more than the invoice total, ignoring payments, so crediting a fully paid invoice shows a negative amount due (money owed back to the client). Raising a credit also never changes the invoice's status. Say if you'd rather cap credits at the remaining balance, or have a credit that clears the balance mark the invoice paid.",
